# MVI Pattern

Every ViewModel follows this structure:

```kotlin
sealed interface FooUiState {
    data object Loading : FooUiState
    data object Empty : FooUiState
    data class Success(val items: List<Item>) : FooUiState
    data class Error(val message: String) : FooUiState
}

sealed interface FooIntent {
    data object Load : FooIntent
    data object Refresh : FooIntent
}

sealed interface FooEvent {
    data object NavigateBack : FooEvent
}

@HiltViewModel
class FooViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val repository: FooRepository,
    private val fooStore: FooStore
) : ViewModel() {

    val uiState: StateFlow<FooUiState> = fooStore.items
        .map { ... }
        .stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5_000), FooUiState.Loading)

    private val _events = Channel<FooEvent>(Channel.BUFFERED)
    val events = _events.receiveAsFlow()

    fun onIntent(intent: FooIntent) { ... }
}
```

## Rules

- UiState, Intent, Event are `sealed interface` (not sealed class)
- Singleton states use `data object`, payload states use `data class`
- One `onIntent(intent)` entry point — no direct public methods for actions
- One-shot events use `Channel<T>(BUFFERED)` + `receiveAsFlow()` (not SharedFlow)
- UiState derived from Store via `combine`/`map` + `stateIn`
- Constructor params are always `private val`

## Error + Empty handling pattern

Always surface errors and distinguish Loading/Empty/Error/Success:

```kotlin
private val _hasLoadedOnce = MutableStateFlow(false)
private val _error = MutableStateFlow<String?>(null)

val uiState: StateFlow<FooUiState> = combine(
    fooStore.items,
    _hasLoadedOnce,
    _error
) { list, hasLoaded, error ->
    when {
        error != null && list.isEmpty() -> FooUiState.Error(error)
        list.isNotEmpty() -> FooUiState.Success(list)
        hasLoaded -> FooUiState.Empty
        else -> FooUiState.Loading
    }
}.stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5_000), FooUiState.Loading)
```

## LoadMore error pattern

Expose pagination errors separately in Success state:

```kotlin
data class Success(
    val items: List<Item>,
    val isLoadingMore: Boolean,
    val loadMoreError: String? = null
) : FooUiState
```
